I've written a SlackBuild but it's not working properly yet.

In the meantime, to run KongArena from your desktop, you can do the following:

0) Download KongArena-Linux-x64.tar.gz from kongarena.com
1) 'tar xf KongArena-Linux-x64.tar.gz' (extract the files as your user) and then, as root, move the resulting kong_arena folder into /opt
2) Put kongarena.desktop in /usr/share/applications/
3) put kongarena in /usr/games and make it executable (chmod a+x)

You should then be able to type 'kongarena' in terminal, or in your desktop menu.

To add controller support, do the following:

0) In kong_arena/bin/extra_args.txt add "-ctrlr kongarena" to the end of the first line
   (e.g. it now says "-nofilter -lowlatency -screen \\.\DISPLAY2 -ctrlr kongarena")
1) Add an empty folder kong_arena/bin/ctrlr
2) Add the file kongarena.cfg to the ctrlr folder, adjusting your joystick buttons as necessary

You can also change options (e.g. key inputs, audio, etc.) directly by running kong_arena/bin/dkwolf_linux 